      "label": "The edit box's shape menu is the browser's own <select>, and the formatted view edits with the browser's editing commands",
      "excerpt": "The edit box's shape menu is the browser's own <select>, and the formatted view edits with the browser's editing commands",
      "text": "Can we get clever and use our own dropdown?  It'll be jarring if that one place in the UI a dropdown looks different.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-03T14:56:21.203Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-03T15:03:17.674Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  the shape menu is now Spell UI's own dropdown (<code>&lt;ui-select&gt;</code>), drawn like every other on the page.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>While at it:  the bar sat under a section's stuck title when the box was a section's first piece;  it's in the top layer now, over it.</li>\n<li>Its menu opens on the bar's solid ground:  the theme's see-through surface let the page show through.</li>\n<li>Merged into main with the rest of P61;  the page server restarted.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ],
